From cd74271e763c95c33660df8d0edcac582ac46375 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harald Ponce de Leon <haraldpdl@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:11:33 +0000
Subject: [Messenger][Doctrine] Make the fetched messages a stopped worker did
 not reach available again

With --fetch-size (and in 8.2 with --concurrency, whose fetch size defaults to the concurrency), Connection::get() marks the whole batch as delivered. When the worker stops before it reaches the rest of the batch (--limit, --time-limit, --memory-limit, a signal), those messages stay hidden until redeliver_timeout. The Doctrine transport now implements CloseableTransportInterface: on close(), which the worker calls once it stopped, it resets delivered_at of the messages it fetched and that were neither acknowledged nor rejected, unless they were delivered again since.
